      "dcDescription": [
        "1969.29.0037 According to the general catalog: Mask, made of bark fabric sent on a wicker frame. The face is made of wood, painted with dark brown color. Decorated with small holes at the eyes, nose and forehead. Between the front and back edge there is a net with holes in the center stretched. Dimensions: front edge-head-back edge: 49cm. Nalandile mask, used by Makishi dancers. The Lozi people. Makishi. Nordrhodesia Rhodesia Zambia Enligt generalkatalogen: Mask, gjord av barktyg uppsänt på vidjestomme. Ansiktet är av trä, målat med mörkbrun färg. Dekorerad med små hål vid ögon, näsa och panna"
